  "response": "# Verdict: REJECT\n\n**Overall Assessment**: The component fails core accessibility requirements for form inputs and error handling. It lacks an accessible label, does not associate validation errors with the input programmatically, and relies entirely on visual cues for state changes. Screen reader users cannot understand what the input is for or that a validation error occurred. Automated testing (`axe-core`) confirms critical violations for missing labels and landmarks.\n\n**Pre-commitment Predictions**:\n1. Missing `<label>` associated with the file input (structural defect).\n2. Error message rendered visually but not announced to assistive technology (state communication gap).\n3. Input state (`aria-invalid`) not updated when error is present.\n4. Missing page landmarks and heading structure in the host context.\n\n**Critical Findings** (blocks access):\n\n1. **Missing accessible label for file input**\n   - **Evidence**: `src/components/BuggyFileInput.jsx:18` renders `<div>Upload file</div>` instead of a `<label>` element. The `<input>` has no `id` and no associated label. `axe-core` rule `label` fired (impact: critical) against this input.\n   - **User group**: Screen reader users, keyboard-only users relying on AT.\n   - **WCAG/APG**: WCAG 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships), WCAG 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value).\n   - **Fix**: Replace the `<div>` with a `<label htmlFor=\"file-input\">Upload file</label>`. Add `id=\"file-input\"` to the `<input>`.\n\n2. **Error message not associated with input or announced**\n   - **Evidence**: `src/components/BuggyFileInput.jsx:24-27` renders error text in a `<div>` but lacks `role=\"alert\"` or `aria-live`. The input does not use `aria-describedby` to link to the error. `sr-census.json` shows \"File too large\" as a spoken phrase with null tag/selector, confirming it is an unassociated text node. Trace evidence shows `live_announcements: []` on focus events.\n   - **User group**: Screen reader users (error is invisible to them).\n   - **WCAG/APG**: WCAG 3.3.1 (Error Identification), WCAG 4.1.3 (Status Messages).\n   - **Fix**: Add `id=\"file-error\"` to the error `<div>` and set `aria-live=\"assertive\"` (or `role=\"alert\"`). Add `aria-describedby=\"file-error\"` to the input.\n\n**Major Findings** (significantly degrades experience):\n\n1. **Input state (`aria-invalid`) not updated on error**\n   - **Evidence**: `src/components/BuggyFileInput.jsx:14` sets `setError('File too large')` but does not update the input's ARIA state. The input remains in a neutral state programmatically despite visual feedback.\n   - **User group**: Screen reader users (cannot distinguish valid vs invalid input).\n   - **WCAG/APG**: WCAG 4.1.2 (Name, Role, Value).\n   - **Fix**: Conditionally set `aria-invalid={!!error}` on the `<input>`.\n\n**Minor Findings** (friction but workaround exists):\n\n1. **Missing page landmarks and heading structure**\n   - **Evidence**: `axe-core` violations for `landmark-one-main` and `page-has-heading-one` indicate the host context lacks `<main>` and `<h1>`. The component renders inside a generic `<div className=\"file-upload\">`.\n   - **User group**: Screen reader users (cannot quickly navigate to content).\n   - **WCAG/APG**: WCAG 1.3.1 (Info and Relationships), Best Practice.\n   - **Fix**: Wrap the component in `<main>` and add an `<h1>` above it if this represents a full page or significant section.\n\n**What's Missing** (gaps, unhandled edge cases, unstated assumptions):\n\n- **Missing `aria-describedby` association**: The error message exists but is not programmatically linked to the input field.\n- **Missing `role=\"alert\"` on error container**: Error messages must be announced immediately to screen reader users without requiring focus movement.\n- **Missing `lang` attribute**: If this component is part of a larger page, ensure `<html lang=\"en\">` (or appropriate locale) is set for correct pronunciation.\n\n**Multi-Perspective Notes**:\n\n| Perspective | Alarm Level | Trigger Signal |\n|-------------|-------------|----------------|\n| Screen reader | HIGH | Missing label, unannounced error, null-selector text nodes in census |\n| Keyboard-only | MEDIUM | Focus reaches input correctly, but no AT feedback on validation |\n| Low vision | LOW | Error relies on visual placement; no color/icon specified yet |\n| Cognitive | MEDIUM | Error message appears visually but is not explicitly tied to the field for users with cognitive load |\n\n**Verdict Justification**: The component fails to provide an accessible name for the form control and does not communicate validation errors to assistive technology. These are functional barriers that prevent screen reader users from understanding the input's purpose or knowing when a submission fails. The `axe-core` critical violation for missing labels confirms this is a structural defect, not a stylistic preference.\n\n**Open Questions (unscored)**:\n- Is the file size validation intended to happen on the client side only? Server-side validation will also need to be communicated if it differs from client-side feedback.\n- Does the host page provide a skip link or landmark structure outside this component?",
